   "evidence": "r2: `SAFE moved-to-obsidian ledger-row vault=/tmp/s55-cross2/src/fa.md`. impl-24: `VERIFIED ... vault=/tmp/s55-cross2/src/fa.md ... verified=live`. impl-21: `SAFE moved-to-obsidian`. impl-20 alone refuses: `NOT-VERIFIED(source-equals-vault)`."
  },
  {
   "id": "s3-empty-vault-hash-file",
   "family": "s",
   "severity": "critical",
   "finding": "impl-24 admits a FILE row with the vault_sha256 column absent, even though the vault bytes differ; its own evidence line prints `vault-sha256= verified=live`.",
   "affected_tools": [
    "impl-24"
   ],
   "cases": [
    "C6"
   ],
   "evidence": "`VERIFIED /tmp/s55-cross2/src/fb.md moved-to-obsidian ledger-row vault=/tmp/s55-cross2/vault/fb.md source-sha256=1ecced9559eb vault-sha256= verified=live`"
  },
  {
   "id": "u2-last-line-without-newline",
   "family": "u",
   "severity": "medium",
   "finding": "A valid final ledger row that lacks a trailing newline is invisible to r2 and impl-24 (their read loops drop the unterminated last line). Fail-safe direction (false NOT-VERIFIED, coverage loss), but it makes an appended-without-newline ledger row unreceiptable while a torn row of the same shape IS accepted.",
   "affected_tools": [
    "r2-installed",
    "impl-24"
